id: dragon-ball
name: Dragon Ball
kind: gear
# A Special Basic Item: only the ARC hands them out, and nothing crafts them.
special: true
# "Dragon Balls come in sets of 2~7 balls." Which set, and which ball of it, asked when it is
# given.
setMin: 2
setMax: 7
# "You may spend all the Actions in your turn (minimum 3) to summon an Eternal Dragon in a
# Combat Encounter."
summonActionsMin: 3
source: Core Rule
description: >
  One of a set of 2 to 7. Gather them all, and every Action in your turn - three at least -
  summons the Eternal Dragon.
text: >
  Dragon Ball: One of the magic dragon balls. You can find them all.
  –Effects: Dragon Balls come in sets of 2~7 balls. Once you gather all of them, you may spend
  all the Actions in your turn (minimum 3) to summon an Eternal Dragon in a Combat Encounter.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Given: how many balls its set has and which of them this one is - named for it, "Dragon Ball
# (3-Star)". A character holding every ball of a set is offered Summon, on the first of them.
#
# Summon: in a Combat Encounter, every Action left in the turn, and three at least; outside
# one, nothing - there are no Actions to count. It is said at the table, and that is all: what
# the Eternal Dragon does is the ARC's.
#
# The balls stay on the character afterwards. Where they scatter to is the story's.
